MacJev-322M-4K-Laya-MLX
Independent experimental model release maintained by chaoliangUNSW.
Native MLX conversion of https://huggingface.co/chaoliangUNSW/MacJev-322M-4K-Laya
(FP32 source weights SHA-256 a1c8cb93485dc32a499cd221dfc9a534dd4e309f5c3ab908ea13d0190a203750).

This work includes portions derived from Laya:
https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya
Upstream source commit: 573e5b62696ba441230cd6be71d593331b5d23af
Model: convaiinnovations/laya, multilingual subfolder
Model revision: 1c5edc17a7acd8701df6fc341c0d179f1c62c982
Laya is licensed under Apache License 2.0; see LICENSE.

The backbone originates from jhu-clsp/mmBERT-base, licensed under MIT;
see MMBERT_LICENSE for the upstream notice. The encoder follows the
ModernBERT architecture as implemented in Hugging Face Transformers.

The MLX runtime is an independent reimplementation of the same computation.
Its packaging follows the approach of community MLX ports of Laya.

Relative to the FP32 release, only the file container and runtime change:
the same float32 tensors are saved with MLX and run by a native MLX
implementation in float32. No retraining, quantization or recalibration.
JEV is comparison/category context only; no JEV weights are included.
